Track 1: Brass Refractors Chew the Smog
- Story & Context: Astrid hauled her grandfather's brass telescope and a water-damaged 1964 Flemish harpsichord onto the bitumen roof of the Purfleet silo, angling her optics through the oily smog to find the Andromeda galaxy. When an outbound chemical tanker unleashed a seventy-hertz blast into the grey soup, she slammed her fuzz pedal and struck a frantic D-minor trill in mechanical retort, causing roosting gulls to drop in panic from the radio antennas. Julian lunged across the wet gravel to capture the second freighter answering across the lock with an open reel-to-reel deck, grafting the nautical call directly into a stuttering 164-BPM chopped break. Above the diesel stink and the roar of the river, Astrid screamed into the talkback mic, "the stars drown first, but the steel still talks back," cementing the sound that launched the estuary scene.
